input: {"questions":[{"question":"monokl is still 100% spec markdown (zero crates, no Cargo.toml, no src/) — there's no implementation to check spec-drift against yet. What should \"our current codebase\" mean for this review?","header":"Review scope","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"monokl's spec only (Recommended)","description":"Treat docs/spec/*.md (Parts 1-7, ~9,400 lines) as the input. Reformulate it into callisto-style semantic-model/ + spec@1 tracks, and formally validate it — same target as our recent edge-case audit, just running through canon/axiom instead of ad hoc agents."},{"label":"The whole orin-axi suite","description":"Also pull in michi (implemented), firkin, lumen, pulse — review how they fit together as one ecosystem, not just monokl in isolation. Much larger scope; only makes sense if the goal is ecosystem-wide consistency, not just monokl."}]},{"question":"How much should I actually do right now versus propose first?","header":"Depth this turn","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Set up structure, then run it (Recommended)","description":"Enable the orin-dx-agent-plugins marketplace for monokl (mirroring callisto's settings.json), scaffold .claude/semantic-model + .claude/specs + .claude/plans, then actually invoke trace/canon to produce the first real semantic-model docs and spec@1 tracks from the existing spec."},{"label":"Just scaffold and explain","description":"Set up the directory structure and enable the plugins, but stop there — write up how the semantic-model/specs/plans layout would map onto monokl's existing spec content, without spending agent budget generating the actual artifacts yet."},{"label":"Just tell me the plan first","description":"No file changes yet — walk through what reformulating monokl's spec into this system would look like (which parts become semantic-model files, which become spec@1 tracks) so you can react before anything is written."}]}]}
